IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Basic Law: Israel as the Nation-State of the Jewish People (חוק־יסוד: ישראל – מדינת הלאום של העם היהודי), Sefer HaChukim 5778 no. 2743, p. 898.
-- Row IL-40, draft, target compiler `main`. NOUNS ONLY: types and nothing else.
-- `-- src:N | ...` comments are generated mechanically by tools/srcquote.py from line N of the deposited consolidation
-- (registers/source-bundle/basic-law-...he.wiki.txt), which tools/compare-official.py checked word for word against the
-- official page (NOTES.md section 3).

§ `Nouns of the Nation-State Basic Law`

§§ `Languages, enactments, calendars, days`

DECLARE `A language` IS ONE OF
    Hebrew
    Arabic
    English
    `Another language`

-- Section 4(a): Hebrew is "the language of the State". Section 4(b): Arabic has "a special status in the State".
DECLARE `A status the Basic Law gives to a language` IS ONE OF
    `the language of the State`
    `a special status in the State`

-- The kinds of enactment the questions turn on. `A law of the Knesset` includes a Basic Law. The kind decides whether a
-- text is "a law" in the sense of Interpretation Law s 3 (NOTES.md fork F4).
DECLARE `A kind of enactment` IS ONE OF
    `a law of the Knesset`
    `a Basic Law`
    `an Ordinance given before the State was established or by the Provisional Council of State`
    `an Order in Council of the Mandate`
    `a regulation`
    `a decision of the Government`
    `an administrative direction`

DECLARE `A calendar` IS ONE OF
    `the Hebrew calendar`
    `the Gregorian calendar`
    `another calendar`

DECLARE `A day the Basic Law speaks of` IS ONE OF
    `Independence Day`
    `Memorial Day for the fallen of Israel's wars`
    `Holocaust and Heroism Remembrance Day`
    `the Sabbath`
    `a festival of Israel`
    `another day`

DECLARE `A standing the Basic Law gives to a day` IS ONE OF
    `the official national holiday of the State`
    `an official memorial day of the State`

-- Sections 5, 6 and 7 put duties on the State and give the person no entitlement of their own.
DECLARE `A duty the Basic Law puts on the State` IS ONE OF
    `to be open to Jewish immigration and to the ingathering of exiles`
    `to endeavour to secure the safety of Jews and of citizens in distress or captivity because of their Jewishness or citizenship`
    `to act in the Diaspora to preserve the bond between the State and Jews`
    `to act to preserve the cultural, historical and religious heritage of the Jewish people among Diaspora Jewry`
    `to act to encourage and promote the establishment and consolidation of Jewish settlement`

§§ `Section 4(c): the status Arabic had before the Basic Law`

-- A provision that gave Arabic a standing before the Basic Law came, as the documents in the bundle show it.
-- `the Basic Law names it` is whether the text of the Basic Law itself names the provision (it names none: NOTES.md section 4).
DECLARE `A provision that gave Arabic a standing before the Basic Law` HAS
    `the instrument`               IS A STRING
    `the provision`                IS A STRING
    `its kind`                     IS A `A kind of enactment`
    `what it does as to Arabic`    IS A STRING
    `the Basic Law names it`       IS A BOOLEAN

-- A status of Arabic that a person says they held, in the facts the person can state.
DECLARE `A status of Arabic held before the Basic Law` HAS
    `it was given in practice`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `an enactment gave it`         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day it was held`          IS A DATE

-- Fork F1: what "a status given in practice" (בפועל) reaches.
DECLARE `A reading of what s 4(c) saves` IS ONE OF
    `only a status given in practice`
    `a status given in practice and a status an enactment gave`
    `what s 4(c) saves is declined`

-- Fork F2: the Basic Law has no commencement section, so "before its commencement" has no day in the text.
DECLARE `A reading of the day the Basic Law commenced` IS ONE OF
    `the day it was passed`
    `the day it was published`
    `the commencement day is declined`
